<title>CANADA: Laidlaw to acquire Vancom School buses.</title>
<headline>Laidlaw to acquire Vancom School buses.</headline>
<dateline>BURLINGTON, Ontario 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Laidlaw Inc said on Monday that its school bus and transit services unit has agreed to buy the school bus operations of Vancom Inc.</p>
<p>Laidlaw said the Oakbrook, Illinois-based Vancom is the largest privately owned school bus company in the United States and will increase Laidlaw's school bus fleet size and passenger services revenue by 10 percent.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to close by February 28, 1997 subject to customary conditions.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
